# README Structure Rule

## Purpose
Ensure all agents and subprojects have a consistent, high-quality README.md for onboarding, usage, and maintenance.

---

## Required README.md Structure
1. Title and (optional) Awesome badge
2. Logo (if available)
3. Short description
4. "Why .cursorrules?" or project purpose section
5. Table of Contents
6. Rules or Features section (with categories if relevant)
7. How to Use section (setup, quick start, usage)
8. Contributing section (how to contribute, code standards, rule references)
9. License section

---

## Update & Maintenance
- README.md must be updated when adding new rules, features, or categories.
- Table of Contents and links must remain accurate and relative.
- When adding new categories, update both the ToC and Rules/Features sections.
- Use clear, concise language and practical examples.

---

## Enforcement
- Meta-agent or reviewers should check for README compliance on PRs and new agent creation.
- Non-compliant READMEs should be flagged for revision before merge.

